# Agent Instructions
Describe this project's purpose, implementation boundaries, and local rules here. Adapt this template; do not leave placeholders as active instructions.

## Workflow source
This project adopts `project-workflows/`. Read its `workflow.toml` for configured document locations, then use its `skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` procedures. The project-specific copy is authoritative over global seeds. Project instructions override seed defaults. General skills and external-service tooling are optional unless explicitly adopted.

## Documentation
README explains the project and how to start. TODO indexes active work. Current policies define standing guidance; spike pairs hold scoped reasoning and work state; scratch is provisional; archives preserve history. Actual project documents live in this repository, outside the workflow submodule.

## Validation and Git
Record the actual validation commands and commit/review policy. Preserve concurrent work. Review scoped diffs before committing; never include private configuration or credentials. Publishing and remote actions follow the user's authorization and repository policy.

## Markdown style
Keep each prose paragraph or comment paragraph on one line and let editors wrap it. Avoid reflow-only edits. Preserve meaningful line breaks, existing local conventions, and explicit formatter requirements.
